Computer Science and Engineering (CSE) is a field that combines computer science, programming, software development, and engineering principles. It focuses on understanding how computers and software systems work and how to develop solutions to real-world problems. CSE students learn subjects such as Data Structures and Algorithms, Object-Oriented Programming, Database Management Systems, Operating Systems, Computer Networks, Web Development, Cloud Computing, Artificial Intelligence, and Machine Learning. Programming languages such as Java, Python, C++, and JavaScript are commonly used to build applications and solve computational problems. CSE also provides career opportunities in areas such as software development, web development, data science, AI/ML, cybersecurity, cloud computing, DevOps, and system design. With strong technical skills, problem-solving ability, communication skills, and practical project experience, a CSE graduate can build a successful career in the technology industry.